# promise: #715
# Settings ▸ Profiles ▸ "Check spelling while typing" turns Chromium's spell check off and on for the
# profile: browser.enable_spellchecking, the pref chrome://settings/languages ▸ Spell check sets. Cra's
# text-field menu has no Spelling and Grammar submenu (Chromium's Mac menu as Cra shows it), so before
# this there was no switch in Cra for it. On by default, as in Chromium.
budget rss=700 stalls50=10
cra://open?url=${PAGE}?n=spell
expect-log loaded 127\.0\.0\.1 \(HTTP 200\)
wait 1
cra://debug?chromePref=browser.enable_spellchecking
expect-log chrome pref browser\.enable_spellchecking: true
cra://debug?spellCheck=state
expect-log spell check setting: on$
cra://debug?spellCheck=off
expect-log spell check off in Default: set$
expect-log spell check setting: off$
cra://debug?chromePref=browser.enable_spellchecking
expect-log chrome pref browser\.enable_spellchecking: false
cra://debug?spellCheck=on
expect-log spell check setting: on$
cra://debug?chromePref=browser.enable_spellchecking
expect-log chrome pref browser\.enable_spellchecking: true
